NNAAMMEE
     bbrraanndd..44tthh — FreeBSD ASCII art boot module

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The file that goes by the name of bbrraanndd..44tthh is a set of commands designed
     to draw the ASCII art BSD brand above the boot loader menu.  The commands
     of bbrraanndd..44tthh by themselves are not enough for most uses.  Please refer to
     the examples below for the most common situations, and to loader(8) for
     additional commands.

     Before using any of the commands provided in bbrraanndd..44tthh, it must be in‐
     cluded through the command:

           include brand.4th

     This line is present in the default _/_b_o_o_t_/_m_e_n_u_._r_c file, so it is not
     needed (and should not be re-issued) in a normal setup.

     The commands provided by it are:

           ddrraaww--bbrraanndd             Draws the BSD brand.

                                  The brand that is drawn is configured by
                                  setting the llooaaddeerr__bbrraanndd variable in
                                  loader.conf(5) to one of “fbsd” (the de‐
                                  fault) or “none”.

                                  The position of the logo can be configured
                                  by setting the llooaaddeerr__bbrraanndd__xx and
                                  llooaaddeerr__bbrraanndd__yy variables in loader.conf(5).
                                  The default values are 2 (x) and 1 (y).

     The environment variables that effect its behavior are:

           _l_o_a_d_e_r___b_r_a_n_d
                     Selects the desired brand in the beastie boot menu.  Pos‐
                     sible values are: “fbsd” (default) or “none”.

           _l_o_a_d_e_r___b_r_a_n_d___x
                     Sets the desired column position of the brand.  Default
                     is 2.

           _l_o_a_d_e_r___b_r_a_n_d___y
                     Sets the desired row position of the brand.  Default is
                     1.

